  "body": "When a chat-lifecycle run fails during finalization, the coordinator currently reports only `finalize` and an unavailable report. The rejecting dataset, snapshot, worker-stop, or output step and its underlying error are lost. Retain a closed set of stage/reason fields and the prior terminal observation in the existing controller diagnostic and CLI summary, while keeping private error causes available through `errors.Is`/`errors.As`.\n\nThe existing report preference, verdict and exit-code decisions, checkpoint state transitions, and JSON-before-Markdown write order remain unchanged. The diagnostics describe an incomplete finalization; they do not grant report validity. Historical batch128 finalization and cloud message-loss causes remain unverified.\n\nValidation uses deterministic controller, recorder, coordinator and CLI boundary tests, including invalid guards, failed continuous hooks, output failures, private-error redaction, and diagnostic-log error/short-write handling. The retained four implementation slices include their original RED/GREEN results; independently requested coverage additions and two rejected continuous-test fixtures are recorded separately. `GOWORK=off go test -json ./internal/bench/chatlifecycle ./cmd/wkcli/internal/benchmark -count=1` passed all 866 top-level tests (1,613 passing events), with no failures or skips.\n\nThe knowledge note also records the independently verified Go 1.25.11 nested-worktree VCS-stamp limitation and clean-source construction procedure. Related: #1025.\n\nIndependent Standards and Spec reviews have no open findings on `3d243bccc8caed21a8719071ad7c1883156713c2`; the Spec coverage finding was closed by seven additional boundary cases.\n",
